# Copy to .env, then fill in:  cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is gitignored. Never commit real values.
#
# This file configures the build and deploy tooling (wrangler, vite).
# Provider API keys do NOT belong here — they belong in packages/agents/.env,
# because that file is what reaches the Worker runtime. See
# packages/agents/.env.example.

# --- Required: pin the Cloudflare account ------------------------------------
#
# Commands that reach Cloudflare (`pnpm dev`, `pnpm deploy:*`) refuse to run
# when this is unset. That is deliberate: without it, wrangler falls back to
# whichever account happens to be logged in on the machine.
#
# Print your account ids:  npx wrangler whoami
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# --- Optional: non-interactive auth ------------------------------------------
#
# Use this instead of an interactive `npx wrangler login`. Create a token with
# the "Edit Cloudflare Workers" template, plus Workers AI permission if you use
# a `cloudflare/...` model.
#
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
